  * [[http://www.dragino.com/products/mother-board.html]]
  * based on the [[docs:techref:hardware:soc:soc.qualcomm.ar71xx#ar9331|Qualcomm Atheros AR9331]] chipset. Thus lot of general information overlaps with the Wiki pages of other [[docs:techref:hardware:soc:soc.qualcomm.ar71xx#ar9331_based_devices|AR9331-based devices]]
  * 16 MB flash, and 64 MB RAM.  
  * designed for makers
    * 11 GPIOs, 
    * 3.3v, 5v power out
    * connectors for a daughterboard, that has access to the sensor inputs, and to the MIPS serial port, and some GPIOs that can be used as a SPI port.
  * sold as an OEM device or offshore development kit
  * comes with OpenWrt loaded, so you should have no difficulty using it. :)

